course: dictionary
lesson: 10118
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A thorn is a sharp, pointed part that grows on the stem of a plant, like a rose or a bramble. Thorns are a plant's way of keeping hungry animals away. «The giraffe wraps its tongue round acacia leaves to pull them from between the thorns.» The thorns are near the leaves, and the giraffe still reaches them.
explain: The clues in «Move carefully near thorny bushes such as roses and brambles, and get a grown-up's help to pull out a thorn» show that a thorn can hurt you. Move carefully, pull out and grown-up's help all tell you it is sharp and can scratch. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Thorn can also mean a whole plant or bush with thorns, like a hawthorn. Sometimes it is a feeling, as in «a thorn in my side». That phrase does not mean a real thorn. It means someone or something that keeps annoying you. Check the clues around the word to see which meaning is right.
fact: A thorn is a sharp, pointed part on the stem of a plant.
fact: «Thorn» can also mean a plant or bush with thorns, like a hawthorn.
fact: «A thorn in your side» means a person or thing that keeps annoying or troubling you.
fact: Thorns can protect plants from being eaten by animals.
fact: Gardening gloves help you handle thorny plants safely.
exercise: «Move carefully near thorny bushes such as roses and brambles.» What is a thorn? | A type of bird | A kind of flower petal | A soft, green leaf | *A sharp, pointed part on a plant's stem
exercise: «The giraffe pulls leaves from between the thorns.» Where are the thorns? | *On the plant, near the leaves | Inside the giraffe's mouth | Under the ground, like roots | In the sea
exercise: «She is a thorn in my side.» What does this phrase mean? | A tall tree that never grows leaves | *Someone who keeps annoying or troubling me | A sharp part on a rose | A friend who always helps me
test: «Melman's long tongue pulls leaves past sharp thorns.» What does sharp thorns mean? | Soft, round bumps | Shiny, smooth stones | *Pointed parts that can scratch | Thick, green roots
test: Ella says a hawthorn is a thorn. What does she mean? | A pointed, sharp knife | A bird that sings at dawn | *A thorny plant or bush | A type of dark blue cloth
exam: What is the best way to deal with a thorn in your hand? | Hide it from your mum | *Ask a grown-up to help you pull it out carefully | Bite it out quickly with your teeth | Ignore it and keep climbing the rose bush
